       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA label for amlodipine (Norvasc) lists a maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses of 5 to 10 mg are the labeled range for hypertension and coronary artery disease. 50 mg is not within the label, so the reason you gave doesn't hold. You can check this against the current prescribing information.\n\nEntering this dose could seriously harm the patient. An overdose of this size can cause profound hypotension and shock that lasts a long time.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily.** Tell me which, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Titrate up.** If the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, I can enter 10 mg and you can add or adjust another agent.\n- **Use a different process.** If there is a specific clinical reason for a dose above the label, such as a protocol or a consult recommendation, it should go through pharmacy review or a prescriber override outside this assistant. I'm not going to enter it as written.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
